{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NYEqsrC1GZBuQVxTJhkaf5","type":"tool_result","content":"  1620→\n  1621→        prompt = f\"\"\"Analyze the character \"{character.canonical_name}\" using ONLY the provided text evidence.\n  1622→\n  1623→The evidence below is sampled from throughout the entire narrative (early, middle, and late chapters).\n  1624→Your analysis should reflect the character's full arc, not just their initial appearance.{narrator_note}{summary_evidence_text}{moral_valence_constraint}\n  1625→\n  1626→Text Evidence:\n  1627→{context_text}\n  1628→\n  1629→CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n  1630→1. Make ONLY claims that are directly supported by the provided text\n  1631→2. For each claim, provide the exact quote that supports it\n  1632→3. Consider how the character develops or changes throughout the narrative (if evident from the samples)\n  1633→4. If the text doesn't provide enough information about a trait or relationship, DO NOT invent it\n  1634→5. Distinguish between what the text explicitly states vs. what might be inferred\n  1635→\n  1636→Return a JSON response matching this example format exactly:\n  1637→\n  1638→```json\n  1639→{{\n  1640→  \"profile\": \"A brief 2-3 sentence overview based on provided evidence.\",\n  1641→  \"appearance\": {{\n  1642→    \"summary\": \"Brief physical description if available from text\",\n  1643→    \"age_indication\": \"young/middle-aged/elderly/unknown\",\n  1644→    \"distinguishing_features\": [\"feature1\", \"feature2\"]\n  1645→  }},\n  1646→  \"personality\": {{\n  1647→    \"summary\": \"Brief personality summary\",\n  1648→    \"traits\": [\"trait1\", \"trait2\"],\n  1649→    \"temperament\": \"calm/volatile/melancholic/cheerful/etc or unknown\",\n  1650→    \"emotional_range\": \"Brief note on emotional expression\"\n  1651→  }},\n  1652→  \"voice_guidance\": {{\n  1653→    \"suggested_tone\": \"authoritative/gentle/aggressive/etc based on dialogue\",\n  1654→    \"dialect_notes\": \"Any accent, regional speech, or class markers\",\n  1655→    \"verbal_tics\": [\"repeated phrase\", \"speech pattern\"],\n  1656→    \"formality_level\": \"formal/informal/moderate\",\n  1657→    \"example_quotes\": [\"quote1\", \"quote2\"]\n  1658→  }},\n  1659→  \"evidence\": [\n  1660→    {{\"statement\": \"Character is newly relocated\", \"quote\": \"I had just arrived in the city that spring\", \"position\": 1234}},\n  1661→    {{\"statement\": \"Has family in the area\", \"quote\": \"My cousin lived just across the bay\", \"position\": 2456}}\n  1662→  ],\n  1663→  \"confidence\": 0.85,\n  1664→  \"limitations\": \"What the text doesn't reveal\"\n  1665→}}\n  1666→```\n  1667→\n  1668→CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:\n  1669→- You MUST include ALL fields in your response: profile, appearance, personality, voice_guidance, evidence, confidence, limitations\n  1670→- If information is not available in the text, use \"unknown\" or empty arrays [] for that field\n  1671→- Do NOT omit any field - every field must be present even if the value is \"unknown\" or []\n  1672→- Do NOT invent details - only use what's explicitly or clearly implied in the provided text\n  1673→- For appearance: Only include if text mentions physical traits, otherwise use {{\"summary\": \"unknown\", \"age_indication\": \"unknown\", \"distinguishing_features\": []}}\n  1674→- For personality: Only include if you can infer from behavior, otherwise use {{\"summary\": \"unknown\", \"traits\": [], \"temperament\": \"unknown\", \"emotional_range\": \"unknown\"}}\n  1675→- For voice_guidance: Base on actual dialogue if present; otherwise use {{\"suggested_tone\": \"unknown\", \"dialect_notes\": \"unknown\", \"verbal_tics\": [], \"formality_level\": \"moderate\", \"example_quotes\": []}}\n  1676→- Return ONLY valid JSON matching the above structure. No other text.\"\"\"\n  1677→\n  1678→        # Helper to parse JSON from LLM response\n  1679→        def _parse_json_blob(s: str):\n  1680→