As midnight strikes, a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death—cloaked in grave-habits and drenched in blood—enters unchallenged, moving slowly through the chambers until confronting Prince Prospero, who, enraged, pursues him with a dagger but collapses dead upon reaching the black room; the figure is revealed to be the plague itself, and one by one, all revelers die as the clock stops and darkness claims the abbey.\"\n    33→    }\n    34→  ],\n    35→  \"characters\": [\n    36→    {\n    37→      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n    38→      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n    39→      \"aliases\": [\n    40→        \"Prospero\"\n    41→      ],\n    42→      \"role\": null,\n    43→      \"appearance\": null,\n    44→      \"personality\": null,\n    45→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    46→      \"descriptions\": [\n    47→        {\n    48→          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a defiant and arrogant noble who isolates himself and a thousand courtiers in a fortified abbey to escape the plague, ultimately meeting his demise after pursuing a mysterious figure believed to be the Red Death. His actions reflect a pattern of harmful disregard for others' lives, culminating in his own death and the mass fatalities of his guests.\",\n    49→          \"source_position\": 11148,\n    50→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    51→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    52→        }\n    53→      ],\n    54→      \"relationships\": {},\n    55→      \"evidence\": [\n    56→        {\n    57→          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero is enraged by the presence of the Red Death figure and demands immediate execution\",\n    58→          \"quote\": \"insult us with this blasphemous mockery? Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n    59→          \"position\": 11148,\n    60→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    61→        },\n    62→        {\n    63→          \"sta